Any weekend day beyond the first week is misclassified. Day -100 leaves a remainder of 5 when divided by 7, which makes it a Saturday, so the correct result is True. It is not a key in the dictionary, so the wrapper calls the stub and the function returns False. Day 12, also a Saturday, and day 13, a Sunday, fail identically. The redefinition only replays stored answers for the checked day numbers and defers to a constant False elsewhere.

